    "name": "E2E Shopify - Discount Codes",
    "type": "automation",
    "notes": {
        "9717c069-a0de-4c98-9264-5832fc336eb3": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 320,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 256,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data & scopes\n\nThe flow provokes all of its own data — no tenant fixtures needed:\n\n1. **Create Discount Code** leaves the code field empty on purpose, so the component generates a random 8-character code. That keeps the run repeatable: Shopify rejects a duplicate discount code, so a hardcoded one would fail on the second run.\n2. **Get Discount Code** looks the generated code up again and the asserts check the price rule terms (title, usage limit, validity window, minimum subtotal) came back with it.\n3. **Cleanup** is the `Make API Call` after `AfterAll`: `DELETE /price_rules/<id>.json`. Deleting the price rule removes its discount code with it — there is no Delete component for discounts yet.\n\nThe custom app token needs the `read_discounts`, `write_discounts`, `read_price_rules` and `write_price_rules` scopes; without the write scopes the create fails and the cleanup leaves the price rule behind."
        }
    }
